 75NI c  Compiled (unevaluated) data set from 2014Xu07:                         
 75NI2c  Phys Rev Lett 113, 032505 (2014)                                       
 75NI c  Compiled by B. Singh (McMaster), July 23, 2014.                        
 75NI c  {+75}Ni nuclide produced in {+9}Be({+238}U,F) reaction with a          
 75NI2c  {+238}U{+86+} beam of 345 MeV/nucleon produced by the RIKEN            
 75NI4c  accelerator complex. Identification of {+75}Ni nuclei was made on the  
 75NI5c  basis of magnetic rigidity, time-of-flight and energy loss of the      
 75NI6c  fragments (|DE-B|r-tof method) using BigRIPS fragment separator and    
 75NI7c  and ZeroDegree Spectrometer (ZDS) at RIBF-RIKEN facility. Based on A/Q 
 75NI8c  spectrum and Z versus A/Q plot. Measured heavy fragment, |b and |g     
 75NI9c  spectra using wide-range active silicon strip stopper array (WAS3ABi)  
 75NIAc  for beta and ion detection, and EUROBALL-RIKEN Cluster array for |g    
 75NIBc  detection. Decay curves were obtained from time differences between    
 75NICc  implantation and correlated |b decays                                  
 75NI  L 0                             331.6 MS  32                             
